  "worked_solution": "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (2t+5)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3}t)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (4{t}^{2}+20t+25)+4{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2} & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t+25 & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t & =0 \\\\ 20t(t+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+5=5 \\\\ y=-2(0)=0 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(5,0,0).$\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(-1)+5=3 \\\\ y=-2(-1)=2 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(-1)=-2\\sqrt{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(5,0,0)$ and $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$",
